---
source: crates/acpilot-cli/tests/cli.rs
expression: stdout(&serve)
---
Serve the daemon and the web UI over HTTP, printing the token once.

One process, serving the same state `/v1` answers from: a browser at the printed URL talks to the
daemon a TUI would attach to, not to a copy of it. Every request needs `Authorization: Bearer
<token>` except the page itself, which a browser cannot give a header to when the address is typed.

The token is printed on the run that creates it, and only then unless `--token` asks for it again: a
secret in a scrollback is still a secret, and printing it on every start puts it there once per
restart.

Usage: acpilot serve [OPTIONS]

Options:
      --http
          Listen on the default loopback port, `127.0.0.1:7777`.
          
          `--bind` chooses another address and implies this one.

      --bind <ADDR>
          The address to bind, for example `0.0.0.0:7777`

      --token
          Print the bearer token even on a run that did not create it

      --profile <DIR>
          Profile directory the daemon serves

      --workspace <DIR>
          Workspace root the daemon serves. Defaults to this directory

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')
